    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45739" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suāvĭor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sāvĭor</span></b> ),
			ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. a.</i> [id.], <i>to
				kiss</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atticam nostram cupio absentem suaviari, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Brut. 14, 53</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Gell. 3, 15, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">os oculosque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat. 9,
					9</span></i>
			.!*? </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>Act.</i> collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suāvĭo</span></b> ,
			āre, Pompon. and Novat. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 474,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suāvĭātus</span></b> , a,
			um, in a pass. signif., <i><span class="en">Fronto Ep. ad M. Caes. 5</span></i>.</div>
